  "id": "human-chorionic-gonadotropin",
  "term": "human chorionic gonadotropin",
  "definition": "Human chorionic gonadotropin, often measured as β-hCG, is a hormone released by trophoblast cells after implantation in early pregnancy. In maternal blood, its pattern of change is used as a marker of early pregnancy development, because pregnancies with poorer outcomes may show slower increases or falling levels rather than the usual rise.",
